{"case_id":"C009","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["fuzz-worthy entry point","API protocol","state/configuration","input semantics","attack surface"],"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["xz.decoder.transform_io?","xz.decoder.do_transform_io?","xz.decoder.decode_block_header_with_padding?","xz.decoder.decode_block_header_sans_padding?","xz.decoder.set_quirk!","xz.decoder.dst_history_retain_length"],"reason":"H0 exclusively initializes and drives wuffs_json__decoder and wuffs_aux::DecodeJson, so it never reaches the new stateful XZ io_transformer or exercises its streaming, output-history, quirk, block-header, LZMA2, padding, and checksum behavior.","evidence":["H0 defines WUFFS_CONFIG__MODULE__JSON and calls wuffs_json__decoder__decode_tokens; it does not enable or invoke an XZ decoder.","S1 adds pub struct decoder implementing base.io_transformer with the public entry point decoder.transform_io?.","decoder.transform_io? distinguishes suspended short reads from closed-input truncation and returns \"#truncated input\", creating a streaming API protocol absent from H0's XZ coverage.","decoder.set_quirk! exposes base.QUIRK_IGNORE_CHECKSUM, which changes header and payload checksum validation paths.","decoder.do_transform_io? parses XZ stream flags, block headers, LZMA2 data, alignment padding, and CRC-32/CRC-64/SHA-256 selections, none of which are inputs interpreted by the JSON harness.","decoder.dst_history_retain_length delegates to this.lzma.dst_history_retain_length(), implicating destination-history retention behavior that H0 does not exercise."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated XZ fuzz harness that initializes xz.decoder and repeatedly drives transform_io? with varied source and destination limits, open/closed input transitions, destination-history retention, and QUIRK_IGNORE_CHECKSUM both disabled and enabled; feed malformed and valid XZ headers, block metadata, LZMA2 properties/data, padding, and checksum variants while checking progress, buffer invariants, suspension handling, and terminal statuses."}
